  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Given that $F(x,y)=(3{x}^{2}-y)\\,i+(2x+{y}^{3})\\,j,$ what is the scalar curl of $F?$",
  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(2x+{y}^{3})-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(3{x}^{2}-y) \\\\  & =2-(-1) \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
